WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.372 --> 00:00:16.459
Anne was sitting with Ruby Gillis in the Gillis' garden watching the sunset.

2
00:00:17.579 --> 00:00:20.861
Over the summer, Anne had spent many pleasant evenings with Ruby.

3
00:00:22.061 --> 00:00:27.724
Anne had watched Ruby grow paler and weaker, and each evening ended a little earlier than the last.

4
00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:35.004
But Ruby was always cheerful and talkative, always chatting about young men and clothes and the latest Avonlea

5
00:00:35.064 --> 00:00:37.245
news, and never mentioned her health.

6
00:00:39.006 --> 00:00:42.608
At the end of every visit, Ruby made Anne promise to visit again.

7
00:00:43.829 --> 00:00:44.429
Once, Mrs.

8
00:00:44.509 --> 00:00:47.651
Lynde complained about Anne's frequent visits to the Gillis' house.

9
00:00:47.671 --> 00:00:53.854
"Every time you go and visit Ruby, you come back looking so tired, Anne," she said.

10
00:00:53.874 --> 00:00:56.896
"It's so sad," Anne said.

11
00:00:57.832 --> 00:01:00.314
"Ruby doesn't seem to realize that she's sick.

12
00:01:01.315 --> 00:01:04.217
I feel as if I'm watching her fight an invisible enemy."

13
00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:11.423
But when Anne went to visit Ruby one evening at the end of summer, Ruby was strangely quiet.

14
00:01:12.424 --> 00:01:16.247
She did not say a word about parties or new clothes or young men.

15
00:01:17.168 --> 00:01:21.892
Ruby sat in her chair on the porch, with a white shawl wrapped around her thin shoulders.

16
00:01:22.913 --> 00:01:26.896
Just beyond the Gillis' house was the church, with the old graveyard beside it.

17
00:01:27.812 --> 00:01:29.833
The moonlight shone on the white stones.

18
00:01:29.853 --> 00:01:36.716
"How strange the graveyard looks by moonlight," said Ruby suddenly.

19
00:01:36.736 --> 00:01:38.396
"How ghostly."

20
00:01:39.317 --> 00:01:39.917
She shuddered.

21
00:01:39.937 --> 00:01:43.719
"Anne, it won't be long now before I'll be lying over there.

22
00:01:44.539 --> 00:01:49.681
You and Diana and everyone else will keep on living and I'll be there in the old graveyard─dead!"

23
00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:51.362
Anne was shocked.

24
00:01:52.282 --> 00:01:53.963
For a few moments, she could not speak.

25
00:01:53.983 --> 00:01:56.444
"You know it's true, don't you?"

26
00:01:56.788 --> 00:01:58.029
said Ruby insistently.

27
00:01:58.049 --> 00:02:02.730
"Yes, I know," answered Anne in a low tone.

28
00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:06.012
"Everybody knows it," said Ruby bitterly.

29
00:02:06.032 --> 00:02:07.853
"I know it.

30
00:02:08.653 --> 00:02:10.514
I've known all summer, but I didn't want to give up.

31
00:02:11.514 --> 00:02:11.994
Oh, Anne!"

32
00:02:12.915 --> 00:02:15.356
Ruby reached out and grabbed Anne's hand pleadingly.

33
00:02:15.376 --> 00:02:17.376
"I'm afraid to die."

34
00:02:17.396 --> 00:02:20.077
"Why are you afraid, Ruby?"

35
00:02:20.458 --> 00:02:21.518
asked Anne quietly.

36
00:02:21.538 --> 00:02:28.506
"Well," Ruby replied, "I believe there is a heaven, and I think heaven must be very beautiful, of

37
00:02:28.606 --> 00:02:31.548
course but Anne, it won't be what I'm used to."

38
00:02:32.509 --> 00:02:36.673
Anne looked at Ruby and said, "I think heaven will be similar to life here.

39
00:02:37.653 --> 00:02:40.196
In heaven, it will just be easier to be good.

40
00:02:41.016 --> 00:02:42.437
Don't be afraid, Ruby."

41
00:02:42.458 --> 00:02:46.561
"I can't help it," said Ruby pitifully.

42
00:02:46.581 --> 00:02:51.065
"Even if what you say about heaven is true, it won't be the same.

43
00:02:51.925 --> 00:02:52.606
It can't be.

44
00:02:52.626 --> 00:02:54.568
I want to go on living here.

45
00:02:55.604 --> 00:02:56.705
I'm so young, Anne.

46
00:02:57.606 --> 00:02:59.908
I've fought so hard to live and it isn't any use.

47
00:03:00.808 --> 00:03:04.111
I have to die─and leave everything I care for."

48
00:03:05.312 --> 00:03:06.153
Anne sat still.

49
00:03:06.913 --> 00:03:08.995
The silence was almost intolerable.

50
00:03:09.896 --> 00:03:14.499
Anne could not tell Ruby comforting lies; everything that Ruby said was horribly true.

51
00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.562
She was leaving everything that she cared for.

52
00:03:17.582 --> 00:03:22.226
"I want to live," Ruby repeated in a trembling voice.

53
00:03:22.246 --> 00:03:24.908
"I want to live like other girls.

54
00:03:25.884 --> 00:03:29.427
I I want to be married, and have babies.

55
00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:34.112
Anne, I couldn't say this to any one but you.

56
00:03:34.132 --> 00:03:36.114
I know you understand.

57
00:03:37.475 --> 00:03:41.699
And then poor Tony Spencer He loves me and I love him, Anne.

58
00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:46.303
The others meant nothing to me, but he does, and if I could live, I would be his

59
00:03:46.363 --> 00:03:48.645
wife. I would be so happy.

60
00:03:48.665 --> 00:03:50.427
Oh, Anne!"

61
00:03:50.867 --> 00:03:51.588
Ruby sobbed.

62
00:03:54.096 --> 00:03:57.038
Anne held Ruby's hand, and offered her silent sympathy.

63
00:03:57.898 --> 00:04:02.001
It was a relief to Anne not to have to use clumsy words, and her silence was a

64
00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.242
deeper comfort to Ruby.

65
00:04:04.282 --> 00:04:07.024
Gradually, Ruby stopped crying and became calm.

66
00:04:07.044 --> 00:04:10.426
"I'm glad I've told you this, Anne," she whispered.

67
00:04:10.446 --> 00:04:13.668
"It has helped me just to speak about it.

68
00:04:14.628 --> 00:04:17.750
I've wanted to talk it over with you for a long time, but I couldn't.

69
00:04:18.751 --> 00:04:20.712
It would have made death seem real.

70
00:04:21.876 --> 00:04:26.419
In the daytime, when people were around me and everything was cheerful, it wasn't that hard to stop

71
00:04:26.459 --> 00:04:27.279
thinking about it.

72
00:04:28.159 --> 00:04:31.481
But at nighttime, when I couldn't sleep, it was so dreadful, Anne.

73
00:04:32.382 --> 00:04:35.403
I would just lie in bed and think about death and get so scared."

74
00:04:36.884 --> 00:04:39.446
Anne said, "Don't be frightened anymore, Ruby.

75
00:04:40.266 --> 00:04:42.467
Just believe everything will be okay."

76
00:04:42.487 --> 00:04:45.169
"I'll try," Ruby replied.

77
00:04:45.189 --> 00:04:47.030
"I try to be brave.

78
00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:49.891
Please come and see me as often as you can."

79
00:04:49.911 --> 00:04:52.336
"I will," Anne replied.

80
00:04:52.356 --> 00:04:56.118
"It it won't be very long now, Anne.

81
00:04:57.038 --> 00:05:01.880
I feel sure of that," said Ruby, "and I'd rather spend time with you than anyone else."

82
00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:05.221
"I must go now, Ruby," Anne said.

83
00:05:05.241 --> 00:05:08.623
"It's getting late, and you shouldn't be out in the cold."

84
00:05:09.443 --> 00:05:11.124
"Goodnight, Anne," said Ruby.

85
00:05:12.284 --> 00:05:14.605
Anne walked home very slowly in the moonlight.

86
00:05:15.466 --> 00:05:17.606
The evening had changed something for her.

87
00:05:18.487 --> 00:05:21.228
Life held a different meaning, a deeper purpose.

88
00:05:22.068 --> 00:05:27.390
It seemed more important to her than ever to live life to the fullest, to love, and not

89
00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:29.730
to be afraid of the challenges that might lie ahead.

90
00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:32.211
Anne never saw Ruby again.

91
00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:38.093
The next morning, the news went from house to house that Ruby Gillis was dead.

92
00:05:39.033 --> 00:05:42.134
She had died in her sleep, painlessly and calmly.

93
00:05:43.114 --> 00:05:48.415
On her face was a smile, as if death had come as a kindly friend instead of the

94
00:05:48.476 --> 00:05:49.856
phantom Ruby had dreaded.

95
00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:52.921
After the funeral, Mrs.

96
00:05:52.981 --> 00:05:55.823
Gillis called Anne aside and gave her a small packet.

97
00:05:55.843 --> 00:06:00.105
"I want you to have this," she sobbed.

98
00:06:00.125 --> 00:06:02.947
"Ruby would have liked you to have it.

99
00:06:04.007 --> 00:06:07.609
It's some embroidery she was doing the afternoon before she died.

100
00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:09.831
It isn't quite finished."

101
00:06:10.871 --> 00:06:12.692
Mrs. Lynde was standing with Mrs.

102
00:06:12.732 --> 00:06:18.796
Gillis. "There's always a piece of unfinished work left," she said with tears in her eyes.

103
00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.043
"But I suppose there's always someone to finish it."

104
00:06:24.084 --> 00:06:28.509
Diana and the residents of Green Gables quietly walked home from Ruby's funeral.

105
00:06:30.471 --> 00:06:33.954
Davy said suddenly, "Ruby Gillis had a great laugh.

106
00:06:34.815 --> 00:06:37.738
Will she laugh as much in heaven as she did in Avonlea, Anne?

107
00:06:38.539 --> 00:06:39.220
I want to know."

108
00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:42.844
"Yes, I think she will," said Anne.
